From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:30:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): give agents tools to raise, update and list
 open items

With open items stored per session, agents need a way to write them: a
label they make up in chat can collide with one used before, and closing
an item means remembering to strike it in a later message.

Three tools in a new open_items tool group, on by default and off with
tool_groups.open_items: false: sys_open_items_raise (one to ten items;
returns each label, the topics in use and the open count; label adopts a
label already written in chat), sys_open_items_update (close with a
resolution, reopen, edit title, detail, topic and links; one result per
label) and sys_open_items_list (compact rows in label order, open and
answered by default). The runner proxies them to the session's
/v1/sessions/{id}/open-items routes with the session as the
orchestration source, so they reach only the calling session; a raise
uses the tool call ID as its idempotency key, so a harness retry gets
the same labels. The group rides the native relay set, so claude-native,
codex-native, pi-native, antigravity-native and hermes sessions get the
tools as SDK harnesses do.

Like the Inbox tools, the runner keeps the group only when the bundle
download says the server stores open items (X-Omnigent-Open-Items: 1);
an older server sends no header and its sessions keep text labels. The
web_fetch researcher turns the group off with the other framework
groups.

Not proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
